#  Rietveld-refined structure for ZnWO4 (sanmartinite)
#  Sample: WO3 + ZnO reacted at 900 C; three-phase Rietveld refinement of
#  Cu K-alpha1/K-alpha2 laboratory powder data (10-100 deg 2-theta).
#  Starting model: COD 1520641 (Dahlborg & Asberg Svensson, Acta Chem. Scand. 53 (1999) 1103)
#  Refined in GSAS-II (see final.gpx).  Overall fit: Rwp = 4.73 %,
#  Rp = 3.63 %, GOF = 1.250, 8301 points, 44 variables.
#  Weight fraction of this phase (normalised over the 3 modelled crystalline
#  phases) = 73.44(17) %   [esd in units of the last digit]
#  Phase Bragg residual R(F) = 1.34 % on 142 reflections.
#  Isotropic displacement parameters were constrained to a single value per
#  phase; for ZnWO4 they are fixed at 0.0050 A^2 (see report.md).
 
######################################################################
data_ZnWO4_Rietveld

# phase info for ZnWO4 follows
_pd_phase_name  ZnWO4
_cell_length_a  4.69248(8)
_cell_length_b  5.72051(10)
_cell_length_c  4.92809(9)
_cell_angle_alpha  90.0000
_cell_angle_beta  90.6349(9)
_cell_angle_gamma  90.0000
_cell_volume  132.279(6)
_symmetry_cell_setting  monoclinic
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M  "P 2/c"
loop_
    _space_group_symop_id
    _space_group_symop_operation_xyz
     1  x,y,z
     2  -x,y,1/2-z
     3  -x,-y,-z
     4  x,-y,1/2+z

